From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] led_controller: Add RGB colour parameters to the core
 configuration

The core configuration carries brightness and a pile of fade timings but has
never had a colour, so there is no way for a caller to ask for anything but
"brighter" or "dimmer". nyx-modules-hybris says so at the point where it hurts:

    /* no nyx params for LED RGB - hence we use grey scale */
    hybris_light_set_pattern(notifications_device, brightness, brightness,
                             brightness, led_on, led_off);

That is not an oversight. The API was modelled on the Palm hardware it shipped
on - board-rib.c on the Pre3 declares the LM8502 channels as keypad,
core_navi_left, core_navi_center and core_navi_right, four single-colour LEDs -
and single-colour hardware needs no colour parameter. Every device LuneOS
supports today has an RGB notification LED, and per-application notification
colours cannot be built without one.

Adds NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_{RED,GREEN,BLUE}, one 0-255 channel
each. Points worth knowing:

- The new values are appended after DIRECTION, so no existing enumerator
  renumbers and a module built against the older header is unaffected.

- A channel defaults to NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_UNSET (-1), not to 0.
  calloc() would have given 0, but 0 is a legal colour - black - and a module
  has to be able to tell "the caller wants this LED off" from "the caller never
  mentioned colour". Only the second case may fall back to the pre-colour
  behaviour, which is what keeps CoreNaviLeds and every other brightness-only
  caller working exactly as before.

- Brightness scales the channels, out = channel * brightness / 255, so
  brightness keeps meaning intensity while colour means hue. The consequence
  worth flagging: brightness is 0 by default for most effects, so setting a
  colour without also setting brightness leaves the LED dark.

- Out-of-range channels are rejected with NYX_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE rather than
  clamped. The surrounding parameters validate nothing at all, but these are
  new, so being strict here cannot break an existing caller.

Colour-blind modules need no change: a module that never asks for these
parameters behaves as it always did.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
  .../client/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration.h | 27 ++++++++++++
  .../nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_common.h | 33 ++++++++++++++
  .../nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_impl.c   | 50 ++++++++++++++++++++++
  3 files changed, 110 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/public/nyx/client/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration.h b/include/public/nyx/client/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration.h
index 7cf5928..03a311a 100644
--- a/include/public/nyx/client/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration.h
+++ b/include/public/nyx/client/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration.h
@@ -332,6 +332,33 @@ NYX_API_EXPORT nyx_error_t nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_create(
  *     brightness,
  *     duration,
  *     direction
+ *
+ *
+ *  Colour - NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_RED,
+ *           NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_GREEN,
+ *           NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_BLUE
+ *
+ *  Accepted alongside any effect above, on the core LEDs only; the backlight
+ *  LEDs ignore it. Each channel is 0..NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_MAX, and
+ *  out-of-range values are rejected with NYX_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE rather than
+ *  clamped.
+ *
+ *  Brightness scales the channels, so brightness keeps meaning intensity and
+ *  the colour keeps meaning hue:
+ *
+ *      out = channel * brightness / NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_MAX
+ *
+ *  Note that brightness is 0 by default for most effects, so setting a colour
+ *  without also setting brightness leaves the LED dark.
+ *
+ *  A channel left at NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_UNSET - the value a fresh
+ *  configuration carries - means the caller expressed no colour preference.
+ *  A module must then behave exactly as it did before these parameters
+ *  existed, which for a single-colour LED is the only thing it can do anyway.
+ *  This is what keeps callers that only ever set brightness working unchanged.
+ *
+ *  Not every LED can honour a colour. A module that drives a single-colour LED
+ *  is free to ignore these, or to derive an intensity from them.
  */
 /**
  * @brief Set a parameter in an LED core configuration.
diff --git a/include/public/nyx/common/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_common.h b/include/public/nyx/common/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_common.h
index c025805..e3d585f 100644
--- a/include/public/nyx/common/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_common.h
+++ b/include/public/nyx/common/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_common.h
@@ -53,6 +53,18 @@ typedef enum
 nyx_led_controller_effect_direction_t;
 
 
+/**
+ * @brief Value a colour channel carries until a caller sets one.
+ *
+ * @see NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_RED
+ */
+#define NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_UNSET (-1)
+
+/**
+ * @brief Largest value a colour channel accepts.
+ */
+#define NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_MAX   255
+
 /**
  * @brief Defines the parameters used by @ref nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_set_param().
  */
@@ -89,6 +101,27 @@ typedef enum
 
 	NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_DIRECTION,       /**< direction */
 
+	/*
+	 * Colour of a core LED, one 0-255 channel per parameter.
+	 *
+	 * Appended after DIRECTION on purpose: every value above keeps the number it
+	 * has always had, so a module built against an older copy of this header
+	 * still resolves the parameters it does know about.
+	 *
+	 * A freshly created configuration carries
+	 * NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_UNSET, meaning the caller expressed no
+	 * preference and the module should keep doing whatever it did before colour
+	 * existed. Where a colour is set, brightness scales it:
+	 *
+	 *     out = channel * brightness / NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_MAX
+	 *
+	 * so a caller that sets a colour has to set BRIGHTNESS too. It defaults to 0
+	 * for most effects, and 0 leaves the LED dark whatever the colour says.
+	 */
+	NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_RED,      /**< colour_red, 0-255 */
+	NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_GREEN,    /**< colour_green, 0-255 */
+	NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_BLUE,     /**< colour_blue, 0-255 */
+
 
 } nyx_led_controller_parameter_type_t;
 
diff --git a/src/device/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_impl.c b/src/device/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_impl.c
index be7ee6b..1101431 100644
--- a/src/device/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_impl.c
+++ b/src/device/nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_impl.c
@@ -57,6 +57,10 @@ typedef struct
 
 	int32_t direction;
 
+	int32_t colour_red;
+	int32_t colour_green;
+	int32_t colour_blue;
+
 	bool final;
 
 } nyx_led_controller_core_configuration;
@@ -77,6 +81,16 @@ nyx_error_t nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_create(
 
 	configuration->final = false;
 
+	/*
+	 * calloc() zeroed these, and zero is a legal colour - black. Every
+	 * effect starts with no colour expressed instead, so that a module can
+	 * tell "caller wants the LED off" from "caller never mentioned colour"
+	 * and keep its pre-colour behaviour in the second case.
+	 */
+	configuration->colour_red = NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_UNSET;
+	configuration->colour_green = NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_UNSET;
+	configuration->colour_blue = NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_UNSET;
+
 	/* common settings */
 	switch (effect_type)
 	{
@@ -217,6 +231,30 @@ nyx_error_t nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_set_param(
 			configuration->direction = new_value;
 			break;
 
+		case NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_RED:
+		case NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_GREEN:
+		case NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_BLUE:
+			if (new_value != NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_UNSET &&
+			        (new_value < 0 || new_value > NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_COLOUR_MAX))
+			{
+				return NYX_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE;
+			}
+
+			if (param == NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_RED)
+			{
+				configuration->colour_red = new_value;
+			}
+			else if (param == NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_GREEN)
+			{
+				configuration->colour_green = new_value;
+			}
+			else
+			{
+				configuration->colour_blue = new_value;
+			}
+
+			break;
+
 		default:
 			break;
 	}
@@ -318,6 +356,18 @@ nyx_error_t nyx_led_controller_core_configuration_get_param(
 			*value = configuration->direction;
 			break;
 
+		case NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_RED:
+			*value = configuration->colour_red;
+			break;
+
+		case NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_GREEN:
+			*value = configuration->colour_green;
+			break;
+
+		case NYX_LED_CONTROLLER_CORE_EFFECT_COLOUR_BLUE:
+			*value = configuration->colour_blue;
+			break;
+
 		default:
 			break;
 	}
